From 2100e476e8f92ee807c2ad3cf8b86ee2c50515ad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yoram <yoram@sifft.io>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 18:30:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] cmake: only require Cdio when ENABLE_OPTICAL is on

ENABLE_OPTICAL=OFF did not actually make optical support optional: Cdio sat
in the unconditional required_deps list, so configure failed with "Could NOT
find Cdio" regardless of the option, and the only way to configure at all
was to build libcdio anyway. The option merely gated the HAS_OPTICAL_DRIVE
and HAS_CDDA_RIPPER defines.

Move the dependency inside the same ENABLE_OPTICAL block that already guards
those defines, so the option controls the requirement too.

This is a backport of how upstream master already does it; the fix landed
after 21.3 was tagged.
---
 CMakeLists.txt | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index 0dc5182fb2..952dc455ca 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -200,7 +200,6 @@ core_require_dep(${required_buildtools})
 
 # Required dependencies. Keep in alphabetical order please
 set(required_deps ASS>=0.15.0
-                  Cdio
                   CrossGUID
                   Curl
                   FFMPEG
@@ -280,6 +279,7 @@ if(ENABLE_UPNP)
 endif()
 
 if(ENABLE_OPTICAL)
+  core_require_dep(Cdio>=0.80)
   list(APPEND DEP_DEFINES -DHAS_OPTICAL_DRIVE -DHAS_CDDA_RIPPER)
 endif()
 
